From: Escapement
Subject: [PATCH] dts: add the AXP2101 PMU, with its battery and USB supplies

The watch's PMU is an X-Powers AXP2101 at I2C 0x34. It is not an AXP20x the
kernel already knows: `drivers/mfd/axp20x-i2c.c` lists axp152/192/202/209/221/
223/313a/323/717/803/806/15060 and nothing else, and mainline has no axp2101
either. patches/kernel/axp2101/ carries the pending "Add support for the
X-Powers AXP2101 PMIC" series (Olivier Louvignes, 2026-10-23) that adds the
variant; this patch gives it something to bind to.

Confirmed on the hardware first, with the BusyBox i2c tools over the bus that
patches/kernel/0001 fixed:

    0x03 = 0x4a      chip ID: AXP2101
    0x34/0x35        battery voltage, 4181 mV
    0xa4 = 0x64      fuel gauge, 100 %

The two child nodes are what userspace sees; without them the PMIC binds but
exposes no supplies:

    /sys/class/power_supply/axp20x-battery
    /sys/class/power_supply/axp20x-usb

## No interrupt node, deliberately

The first version wired the PMIC's IRQ line (GPIO7) as
`interrupts = <7 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_LOW>`. It hung the boot: the log stopped at
"AXP20x variant AXP2101 found" and never reached init, and the console went
silent with the CPU sitting in platform_idle between storms.

The cause is a level-triggered interrupt on a pin that nothing pulls up. The
pinctrl block configures pull-ups for the I2C pins (3 and 2) and nothing else,
so GPIO7 floats; a floating line read as asserted re-fires forever, and that
storm is what starved both the console and the bit-banged I2C bus -- the same
run also produced `i2c-0: sendbytes: NAK bailout` and a failed RTC probe.

Dropping the interrupt makes everything work:

    axp20x-i2c 0-0034: AXP20X variant AXP2101 found
    axp20x-i2c 0-0034: AXP20X driver loaded
    axp20x-regulator axp20x-regulator.0: regulators node not found

Polling is sufficient for battery and charge state, which is what userspace
reads from sysfs anyway. Re-adding the IRQ needs the pin pulled up first, and
is only worth doing for wake-from-sleep.

`regulators node not found` is expected: no regulators node is supplied, so the
regulator driver unloads and the PMU provides only the two supplies.
--- a/arch/xtensa/boot/dts/esp32s3-devkit-c1.dts
+++ b/arch/xtensa/boot/dts/esp32s3-devkit-c1.dts
@@ -33,6 +33,24 @@
 			interrupts = <1 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_FALLING>;
 			wakeup-source;
 		};
+
+		/* X-Powers AXP2101 PMU: battery, charging, and the power rails.
+		 * Its IRQ line is GPIO7 on this board. The two power-supply
+		 * children are what userspace sees as
+		 * /sys/class/power_supply/{axp20x-battery,axp20x-usb}.
+		 */
+		pmic@34 {
+			compatible = "x-powers,axp2101";
+			reg = <0x34>;
+
+			battery {
+				compatible = "x-powers,axp2101-battery-power-supply";
+			};
+
+			usb_power: usb-power {
+				compatible = "x-powers,axp2101-usb-power-supply";
+			};
+		};
 	};
 };
 
